problems.problem:
Prove that there is no finite set containing more than $2N$ ($N > 3$) pairwise non-collinear vectors in the plane with the following two properties:

1) for any $N$ vectors of this set there are $N - 1$ further vectors of this set such that the sum of all $2N - 1$ vectors is zero;

2) for any $N$ vectors of this set there are $N$ further vectors of this set such that the sum of all $2N$ vectors is zero.
